{
  "item": [
    {
      "id": "f5d3197e-c8bc-4c1d-8909-111283d4069d",
      "name": "auth",
      "description": {
        "content": "\nOpenverse provides free and open access to the Openverse API to\nanonymous and registered users. [Refer to the API documentation\nsite for information on how to register](https://api.openverse.org/v1/#tag/auth).\n\nAll Openverse API users are subject to rate limits and restrictions\non how much of Openverse's dataset can be accessed through the API.\n[Individuals should contact Openverse to request expanded access to\nthe API](https://github.com/WordPress/openverse#keep-in-touch).\nRequests are considered on a case-by-case basis and are subject to\nevaluation in light of [Openverse's Terms of Service](https://docs.openverse.org/terms_of_service.html).\nEscalated access may be revoked at any time.\n\nTo authenticate yourself, you must sign up for an API key using\nthe `register` endpoint and then get an access token using the\n`token` endpoint. Read on to know about these endpoints.\n\nIn subsequent requests, include your access token as a bearer\ntoken in the `Authorization` header.\n\n```\nAuthorization: Bearer <access_token>\n```\n\n### Rate limits\n\nOpenverse endpoints are rate limited. Anonymous requests should be\nsufficient for most users. Indeed, https://openverse.org itself\noperates using anonymous requests from the browser.\n\nRegistered users are automatically granted slightly higher limits.\nFurther increases to rate limits are available upon request (see above).\n\nEvery Openverse API response that was subject to rate-limits includes\nheaders outlining the permitted and available usage. Exceeding the limit\nwill result in '429: Too Many Requests' responses.\n\n### Pagination\n\nOpenverse's dataset is valuable, and the\n[Terms of Service](https://docs.openverse.org/terms_of_service.html)\ndisallow scraping under all circumstances. As such, pagination\nfor anonymous users is limited, accommodating only the typical\nusage on https://openverse.org. Pagination is limited in terms\nof the size of individual pages and the total number of works\nvisible for a query (pagination depth).\n\nAuthenticated users are subject to the same limit of total works\navailable for a query, but may request larger individual pages.\n\nIncreases to pagination limits on page size and total depth are\navailable upon request (see above).\n",
        "type": "text/plain"
      },
      "item": [
        {
          "id": "8fa7a1af-e750-4993-994b-4c3fceae0792",
          "name": "register",
          "request": {
            "name": "register",
            "description": {
              "content": "Register an application to access to API via OAuth2.\n\nUpon registering, you will receive a `client_id` and `client_secret`,\nwhich you can then use to authenticate using the standard OAuth2 flow.\n\n> ⚠️ **WARNINGS:**\n> - Store your `client_id` and `client_secret` because you will not be\n>   able to retrieve them later.\n> - You must keep `client_secret` confidential, as anybody with your\n>   `client_secret` can impersonate your application.\n\nYou must verify your email address by click the link sent to you in an\nemail. Until you do that, the application will be subject to the same\nrate limits as an anonymous user.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "auth_tokens",
                "register",
                ""
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [],
              "variable": []
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "description",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "(Required) A description of what you are trying to achieve with your project using the API. Please provide as much detail as possible!"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "email",
                  "value": "<email>",
                  "description": "(Required) A valid email that we can reach you at if we have any questions about your use case or data consumption."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "name",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "(Required) A unique human-readable name for your application or project requiring access to the Openverse API."
                }
              ]
            }
          },
